# Copy to .env and fill in ONE of the three setups below.
# .env is gitignored and is never committed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. OpenAI (or any provider that serves the OpenAI API at the default host)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPENAI_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. A self-hosted or third-party OpenAI-compatible server
#    vLLM, Ollama, llama.cpp, TGI, LM Studio, OpenRouter, Together, Groq,
#    or an internal gateway. Set the URL and the name the server serves the
#    model under. Many local servers ignore the key, but the client still
#    requires a non-empty value — any placeholder works.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MONEYGRAPH_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# MONEYGRAPH_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-32B-Instruct
# MONEYGRAPH_API_KEY=local
#
#   vLLM       python -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server --model <hf-id>
#              -> http://localhost:8000/v1
#   Ollama     ollama serve
#              -> http://localhost:11434/v1   (MONEYGRAPH_MODEL=llama3.1:8b)
#   LM Studio  -> http://localhost:1234/v1
#
# For a self-hosted model also set `llm.api: chat` in config.yaml, and clear
# `llm.reasoning_effort` unless the server accepts that parameter.
# Add its rates under `llm.pricing` in config.yaml, or the run reports
# `unpriced` rather than inventing a number. A local model is free: set
# input/output to 0 and the tracer will report $0.00 honestly.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. No model at all
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every agent has a deterministic fallback, so the pipeline, all three CSVs and
# the whole viewer work with no key. Force it with:
# MONEYGRAPH_NO_LLM=1
#
# Or reuse a previous run's results without recomputing anything:
#   ./agent_run.sh --use-existing
